{% macro fact_sheet(facts) -%}
FACT SHEET (definite outcomes; the narrative may not contradict them: do not show a winner as defeated or a god who acted as silent; bind every deed to the one who REALLY did it, never give a son's deed to the creator or to another son; do not merge events with different doers or kinds into one; do not change the numbers):
{% if facts.creator.deed_count %}
- {{ facts.creator.name }} (the creator, id {{ facts.creator.id }}, ref {{ facts.creator.ref }}) intervened {{ facts.creator.deed_count }} times this age: {{ facts.creator.deeds | join("; ") }}. Do not tell them as silent or distant.
{% else %}
- {{ facts.creator.name }} (the creator, id {{ facts.creator.id }}) did not intervene this age.
{% endif %}
{% for outcome in facts.outcomes %}
- OUTCOME ({% if outcome.kind == "duel" %}duel{% elif outcome.kind == "god_conflict" %}conflict of gods{% else %}war{% if outcome.contest %}: {{ outcome.contest }}{% endif %}{% endif %}, ref {{ outcome.ref }}): {{ outcome.winner }} (id {{ outcome.winner_id }}) WON, {{ outcome.loser }} (id {{ outcome.loser_id }}) LOST{% if outcome.score %}, by {{ outcome.score }}{% endif %}.
{% endfor %}
{% for draw in facts.draws %}
- {{ draw.son }} drew essence from their own source ({{ draw.text }}); this is a separate event from the creator drawing essence.
{% endfor %}
{% if facts.rejected %}
- REJECTED BY FATE (they do not exist; never mention them): {{ facts.rejected | join(", ") }}.
{% endif %}

MANDATORY COVERAGE (each is told at least once, in the main narrative or in its own world's section, by name, with its doer and its outcome; do not list them, bind the events together):
Sons:
{% for son in facts.sons %}
- {{ son.name }} (id {{ son.id }}, ref {{ son.ref }}{% if son.world %}, {{ son.world }}{% endif %}): {% if son.deeds %}{{ son.deeds | join("; ") }}{% if son.deed_count > son.deeds | length %} ({{ son.deed_count }} deeds in all){% endif %}{% else %}did no great deed this age (tell of their waiting in one sentence){% endif %}{% if son.records %}; made or blessed: {% for record in son.records %}{{ record.name }} (id {{ record.id }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% if facts.histories %}
Histories under way this age (the incidents of this age belong to them; tell events as parts of the history they belong to):
{% for history in facts.histories %}
- {{ history.name }} ({{ history.kind }}, since age {{ history.since }}{% if history.ended %}, ended in age {{ history.ended }}{% endif %}{% if history.within %}, part of {{ history.within }}{% endif %})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if facts.events %}
Major events:
{% for event in facts.events %}
- [{{ event.category | replace("_", " ") }}{% if event.world %}, {{ event.world }}{% endif %}] (ref {{ event.ref }}) {{ event.text }}{% if event.repeats > 1 %} (this age {{ event.repeats }} times){% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if facts.tales %}
Tales under way in lives this age (tell their events as parts of these tales):
{% for tale in facts.tales %}
- {{ tale.subject }}: a tale of {{ tale.template }}, now at its {{ tale.stage }}{% if tale.outcome != "open" %}, ended {{ tale.outcome }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if facts.payoffs %}
Payoffs this age (each pays off what was set up in an earlier age; tell it as that payoff):
{% for payoff in facts.payoffs %}
- the {{ payoff.kind }} set up in age {{ payoff.since }}{% if payoff.subject %} about {{ payoff.subject }}{% endif %}: {{ payoff.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if facts.verdicts %}
Fate's verdicts of the previous age (their consequences live in this age; mention each):
{% for verdict in facts.verdicts %}
- (ref {{ verdict.ref }}) {{ verdict.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

COVERAGE FIELD: in "coverage" list the ref of every item above that the text tells, the ids of the records it names, the winner it gives every contest it tells, whom it credits with every listed record it attributes, the gods it presents as silent or idle, and every number it states about an item. The ids and refs go only into "coverage", never into the text.
{%- endmacro %}
